[Music]  The Breakfast Club made stars out of its  young cast including Judd Nelson as  criminal and resident bad boy John  bender since his brat pack days Nelson  has been keeping plenty busy with film  and television appearances here's what  he's been up to throughout the years  many audiences might think that Nelson's  first film appearance was in The  Breakfast Club but it wasn't he appeared  in three films before The Breakfast Club  Rock &amp; Roll Hotel making the great and  Fandango Rock &amp; Roll Hotel has largely  been lost a time but some 80s movie  goers may recognize Nelson from the  second two titles in 1984 is making the  grade  Nelson played a small-time con artist  who must impersonate a rich prep school  kid to earn $10,000 in 1985 spent dango  he played a nerdy member of a group of  college friends who takes one last trip  before graduation cast also included a  young Kevin Costner in his first  starring role the film however failed at  the box office  though Nelson had yet to find much  success in the film world both making  the grade and Fandango set him up  perfectly for his next project Judd  Nelson's big breakthrough came in 1985  with writer director John Hughes The  Breakfast Club the cast included Molly  Ringwald Ally Sheedy Anthony Michael  Hall Emilio Estevez and Nelson as high  school students stuck in saturday  detention it's really not even close by  good you got one more right there The  Breakfast Club was a smash hit making  instant stars out of each of the five  main actors including Nelson later that  year he rejoined many of his cast  members in Joel Schumacher's st. Elmo's  fire that film about recent Georgetown  University graduates added to me more  and Rob Lowe to the cast that also  included Sheedy &amp; Estevez the stars of  these films became so immediately  notorious that a New York magazine  reporter coined the term the brat pack  after seeing some of the young actors  get mobbed in public none of the actors  including Nelson liked the label but the  term inspired by Sinatra's Rat Pack  stuck for years to come and remains  associated with many of them today even  though Nelson never officially returned  to the brat pack throughout his next  series of film and television  appearances he would occasionally  night with some of his former co-stars  in 1986 Nelson lent his voice as hot rod  and Rodimus Prime to the cartoon  Transformers the movie which has since  become a cult classic despite a poor  box-office performance after retaining  with fellow brat Packer Ally Sheedy in  the 1986 revenge drama blue city Nelson  took a different approach by appearing  in the universally praised dear America  letters home from Vietnam a documentary  where actors read correspondences from  the war he then starred in the two-part  NBC TV movie billionaire boys club which  earned Nelson a Golden Globe nomination  for his leading role ultimately he  finished out the 1980s with a few other  film appearances including the roadtrip  film never on Tuesday which also  featured Emilio Estevez Nelson stayed  quite busy throughout the 1990s thanks  to a long stretch of film and television  work after working with famed actor Max  von Sydow in the world war ii inspired  hiroshima out of the ashes he played the  worst comedian in recorded history  in the dark backward following that he  appeared in Mario Van Peebles 1991  gangster film New Jack city  which co-starred rapper turned actor  ice-t as ice tea's partner on a police  investigation Nelson found both  commercial and critical success 1994  gave Nelson a chance to flex his comedy  chops alongside a young Adam Sandler in  airheads the film received mostly  negative reviews from critics but has  since gained cult following in some  circles close out the 90s Nelson  returned to the gangster genre with the  1990 film lighted up appearing as a high  school history teacher who helps  troubled teens during the 1990s Nelson  took a bit of a breather from his film  work to take a starring role in the hit  sitcom suddenly Susan premiering in  September of 1996 suddenly Susan starred  Brooke Shields as a newly single  magazine writer Nelson played the role  of Susan's boss Jack Richmond moving  away from his 80s bad-boy image Nelson  got the stretch his acting muscles as  Jack by building on story arcs involving  his character's troubled marriage  suddenly Susan was a ratings hit in its  first season but lost viewers by season  two and never fully recovered  Nelson left the show at the beginning of  season 4  throughout the 2000s Nelson appeared in  a number of recurring stints on  television shows including spots on both  CSI and CSI in New York Las Vegas the  Outer Limits and the detective comedy  psych he also snagged a recurring guest  role as a comically jealous ex-husband  on the eighth season of Two and a Half  Men coincidentally Nelson appeared  alongside Charlie Sheen on the series  the brother of his fellow brat Packer  Emilio Estevez thanks to his signature  role as John bender Nelson was also able  to snag some roles in the beginning of  the 21st century in addition to making a  significant cameo in Jay and Silent Bob  strike back nelson revived the bender  character for an uncredited role in the  Star Wars themed Family Guy episode blue  harvest any questions yeah I got a  question does Barry Manilow know you  raid his wardrobe throughout the 2000s  and 2010's Nelson kept up his career in  both film and television mixing  made-for-tv movies with Studio  productions and animated shows he  returned to the Transformers franchise  in 2009 playing Rodimus Prime for the  Cartoon Network series while also  voicing multiple roles for the animated  series Ben 10 omniverse Nelson has also  dabbled in hallmark films including  Santa Junior in 2002 and 2010's canceled  Christmas in the latter film he plays  Chris Frost who is of course secretly  Santa Claus  in 2009 he appeared in the sequel The  Boondock Saints to All Saints Day much  like its predecessor however the sequel  is met with negative reviews Nelson's  biggest starring role in the 2000s was  the television movie cabin by the lake  it aired on the USA Network in 2000 and  starred Nelson as a screenwriter who  moonlights as a serial killer the  following year he starred in a sequel  return to cabin by the lake though  neither film fared particularly well  with critics in recent years Nelson has  sought out new and challenging roles and  some of televisions most interesting  shows in 2013 during the fourth and  final season of Nikita  Nelson played a deep-cover operative  unknowingly working for the terrorist  organization known as the shop Nelson  later took a role on the hugely popular  hip hop drama Empire in the show's  wildly  successful first season Nelson played a  cutthroat and competitive CEO named  Billy beretti thanks to the show's major  success Nelson found himself back in the  spotlight and with a great new credit to  boot check out one of our newest videos  right here plus even more looper videos  about your favorite actors are coming  soon subscribe to our YouTube channel  and hit the belt so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]

